{"game": "drg-rogue-core", "language": "english", "appid": 2605790, "month": "2026-08", "window": 4, "start_date": 1787529600, "end_date": 1788220799, "month_true_total": 242, "quota": 9, "returned": 9, "pulled_at": "2026-09-02 11:06:50 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "234194566", "author": {"steamid": "76561198041246790", "personaname": "Virixiss", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/virixiss/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 17, "playtime_forever": 630, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 630, "last_played": 1779682177, "avatar": "d7e24ac9b430985fa194dade39c63ca22885ab0a"}, "language": "english", "review": "I excitedly waited on this game for like 3 years. And what I got was honestly kind of bland. What I wanted was a roguelite DRG, something where you need to go in, scrounge for needed upgrades, explore every nook and cranny for resources, experiment with gear that you found or new skills to equip, clear a big bossfight at the end, then return with all your phat loot. And DRG:RC kinda gives you that but, almost none of it is fully baked or thought through. Class identity doesn't exist because almost every upgrade is generic across all classes. All builds are functionally going all in on your class ability or going all in on a single gun. The hordes in this horde shooter are tedious and painful at a certain point, and many of the guns have no actual use in this game except number padding.\n\nMy most major gripe with the game: The timer punishes you for staying in a level for too long. Almost every roguelike or roguelite that I've played encourages you to keep moving at a good pace, but never have I had one actively punish you for exploration and completion like Rogue Core does. At a certain point, the agreed upon tactic is to bascially rush the \"gimme\" upgrades and skip literally everything else. Having your community come to the conclusion that skipping massive parts of your game in order to not be bent over by an arbitrary timer is a damning state to see.\n\nI have faith that GSG will turn this around. The game has bones, but no meat and no fat at the moment. Genuinely at this point, Far Far West does what Rogue Core wants to do, but way better so until RC gets a fair number of updates, I'd invest my time there instead.", "timestamp_created": 1788213483, "timestamp_updated": 1788213483, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1779292819", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "234193874", "author": {"steamid": "76561197988578942", "personaname": "Hoizen", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Hoizen/", "num_games_owned": 544, "num_reviews": 16, "playtime_forever": 233, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 233, "last_played": 1779589562, "avatar": "4957951f504af27e35c8d960451c93550bebc178"}, "language": "english", "review": "I just didn't feel like there was any reason to play this over deep dives in DRG? I just felt confused why I was playing this as I did not get any kind of different fun compared to doing more DRG nor was it as fun as DRG. \r\n\r\nI'll try again in the future... but I've been unable to feel interested to launch it again after a few runs.", "timestamp_created": 1788212865, "timestamp_updated": 1788212865, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.53271031379699707", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1779292819", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "234181061", "author": {"steamid": "76561198132683803", "personaname": "Fokker", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "